{"timestamp":"2025-07-09T20:45:20.297Z","level":"ERROR","pid":4080,"message":"Response content:","metadata":"<think>\nOkay, I need to create a comprehensive test script based on the user story provided. The user wants to go to the website https://sanp-fill.vercel.app/ and log in with the username \"manish-9211\" and password \"kaku\". They specified to only fill the password they provided.\n\nFirst, I'll start by understanding the HTML content and available selectors. The login form has a username input with id \"username\" and a password input with id \"password\". The form submission is handled via JavaScript, which sends a POST request to /api/auth/login. If the credentials are invalid, an error modal appears with an error message.\n\nThe available selectors are:\n- Username input: #username\n- Password input: #password\n- Login button: button[type=\"submit\"]\n- Error modal: #errorModal\n- Close button in error modal: .close-btn\n\nNow, I'll outline the test steps. The test should navigate to the URL, fill in the username and password, submit the form, and check if the login is successful or if an error is displayed.\n\n1. Navigate to the URL.\n2. Wait for the form to load. I'll check for the username input to ensure the page is ready.\n3. Type the username into the username field.\n4. Type the password into the password field.\n5. Click the login button.\n6. After submission, check if the error modal appears. Since the credentials are likely invalid, the error should show up.\n7. Assert that the error message is displayed correctly.\n8. Close the error modal by clicking the close button.\n9. Finally, check that the modal is no longer visible after closing.\n\nI need to include proper waits and assertions. Using explicit waits for elements to be present or visible is better than implicit waits. I'll use timeouts of 30 seconds for each step, which is reasonable for most web applications.\n\nFor the assertions, I'll check if the error modal is present after form submission and if it becomes invisible after closing.\n\nPotential errors to handle include elements not loading on time, which can be mitigated with waits. The test should gracefully handle such issues by waiting for elements before interacting with them.\n\nI'll structure the test steps in JSON format as specified, including setup (navigation) and teardown (no specific steps needed here, but closing the modal can be part of the steps).\n\nI should also ensure that the test doesn't proceed if any step fails, so each action should be sequential with proper error handling in the code, but in the JSON, it's more about the correct order.\n\nFinally, I'll make sure the test script is comprehensive, covering all necessary interactions and assertions to validate the user story.\n</think>\n\n```json\n{\n  \"title\": \"Login Test with Username and Password\",\n  \"description\": \"Test the login functionality with provided credentials and verify error handling.\",\n  \"url\": \"https://sanp-fill.vercel.app/\",\n  \"steps\": [\n    {\n      \"action\": \"navigate\",\n      \"selector\": \"\",\n      \"description\": \"Navigate to the login page\",\n      \"timeout\": 30000\n    },\n    {\n      \"action\": \"wait\",\n      \"selector\": \"#username\",\n      \"description\": \"Wait for the username input to be present\",\n      \"timeout\": 30000\n    },\n    {\n      \"action\": \"type\",\n      \"selector\": \"#username\",\n      \"description\": \"Enter the username\",\n      \"timeout\": 30000,\n      \"value\": \"manish-9211\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"action\": \"type\",\n      \"selector\": \"#password\",\n      \"description\": \"Enter the password\",\n      \"timeout\": 30000,\n      \"value\": \"kaku\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"action\": \"click\",\n      \"selector\": \"button[type=\\\"submit\\\"]\",\n      \"description\": \"Submit the login form\",\n      \"timeout\": 30000\n    },\n    {\n      \"action\": \"wait\",\n      \"selector\": \"#errorModal\",\n      \"description\": \"Wait for the error modal to appear\",\n      \"timeout\": 30000\n    },\n    {\n      \"action\": \"assert\",\n      \"selector\": \"#errorModal\",\n      \"description\": \"Verify error modal is displayed\",\n      \"timeout\": 30000,\n      \"expected\": \"displayed\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"action\": \"click\",\n      \"selector\": \".close-btn\",\n      \"description\": \"Close the error modal\",\n      \"timeout\": 30000\n    },\n    {\n      \"action\": \"wait\",\n      \"selector\": \"#errorModal\",\n      \"description\": \"Wait for the error modal to disappear\",\n      \"timeout\": 30000\n    },\n    {\n      \"action\": \"assert\",\n      \"selector\": \"#errorModal\",\n      \"description\": \"Verify error modal is no longer displayed\",\n      \"timeout\": 30000,\n      \"expected\": \"not displayed\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"assertions\": [\n    {\n      \"action\": \"assert\",\n      \"selector\": \"#errorModal\",\n      \"description\": \"Error modal should be present after invalid login attempt\",\n      \"expected\": \"present\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"action\": \"assert\",\n      \"selector\": \"#errorModal\",\n      \"description\": \"Error modal should not be present after closing\",\n      \"expected\": \"not present\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```"}
