{"timestamp":"2025-07-25T09:53:13.035Z","level":"INFO","pid":24888,"message":"<think>\nOkay, I need to create a comprehensive test script based on the user's story. Let me start by understanding the user's requirements. The user wants to click the login button, fill out the login form with username 'manish-9211' and password 'kaku', and then click the delete question button upon reaching the dashboard.\n\nFirst, I'll look at the available selectors provided. The username and password fields have unique name attributes, so their selectors are straightforward: input[name='username'] and input[name='password']. The login button has a class 'login-button', so the selector is .login-button. The delete question button has a class 'delete-question', but it's nested within a div with class 'question-actions', so the selector is .question-actions .delete-question.\n\nNow, I'll outline the test steps. The test should start by navigating to the login page. Then, it should fill in the username and password. After that, click the login button. Once logged in, it should navigate to the dashboard, wait for the delete button to appear, and then click it. Finally, it should log out and close the browser.\n\nI need to include proper waits and assertions. For each action, I'll add a wait to ensure elements are present before interacting with them. For example, after navigating to the login page, wait for the username field to be present. After clicking login, wait for the dashboard to load by checking for the delete button.\n\nI should also handle potential errors gracefully. Using timeouts appropriately will help avoid issues if elements take time to load. Each step should have a meaningful description so that anyone reading the test can understand what's happening.\n\nFor the assertions, I'll check if the username and password fields are present on the login page and if the delete button is present on the dashboard. This ensures that the test doesn't proceed if any critical elements are missing.\n\nI'll structure the JSON with a title and description, the starting URL, an... [truncated]"}
